  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement concerns an evidence gap about the measure, rather than competing interpretations of the balance formula. Independent inspection of the native supplement resolves that gap. The classification is faithful-equivalent under the recorded user-adopted interpretation only.",
      "primary_evidence": "The round-trip judgment identifies D065 as its substantive blocker. The supplied explicit Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id declaration identifies @MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume Real Real.measureSpace with StieltjesFunction.id.measure. The target and D001 preserve the adopted rectangle conditions and intervalwise almost-everywhere rate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested measure investigation is resolved from declaration content, without relying on a prior verdict or treating provenance hashes as semantic proof. The selected measure has ordinary real length normalization and the intended null sets.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement expands Real.measureSpace to measureSpaceOfInnerProductSpace with Real.measurableSpace and Real.borelSpace; Real.measurableSpace is borel Real. Its explicit volume identity and volume_Ioc declaration concern the same Real.measureSpace used by the target."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The reason for withholding a classification is removed by the supplementary declaration evidence. The remaining printed-source ambiguity is preserved as a limitation of source-only comparison, not an unresolved dependency of this interpreted task.",
      "primary_evidence": "The attached printed pages 4–5 leave discontinuity derivative semantics unspecified. The separate receipt explicitly adopts rectangle conservation with integrability and interval-dependent almost-everywhere mass rate. The elaborated target expresses those conditions using the measure identified in the supplement."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D065 unclear",
      "resolution": "D065 is understood with the supplement: its distinguished measure is the identity Stieltjes measure on the Borel real line, with ordinary length normalization. The blind translator's caution was justified by its narrower packet but does not remain a blocker in the complete adjudication evidence.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement supplies the explicit selected instance, Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id, StieltjesFunction.id with toFun := id, and StieltjesFunction.measure_Ioc giving ENNReal.ofReal (f b - f a). The fully explicit Real.volume_Ioc specializes this to ENNReal.ofReal (b - a) for the target's exact volume expression."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Conclusion completeness passes under the recorded interpretation. The theorem retains the rectangle balance and integrability while explicitly asserting the time derivative of spatial vector mass with the correct endpoint flux difference, almost everywhere for each fixed spatial interval.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.10) on printed page 4 differentiates the spatial integral and uses first-endpoint flux minus second-endpoint flux. The target's final conjunct is ∀ a b, ∀ᵐ t, HasDerivAt (fun s => ∫ x in a..b, q x s) (flux (q a t) - flux (q b t)) t. D065 is resolved by the native supplement."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Operator interpretation passes. D001 contains precisely the two integrability requirements and rectangle balance. D018 and D083 give interval integrability and oriented vector integration; D015 gives an actual derivative; D011 and D027 place it outside a null set. The identified measure supplies ordinary spatial and temporal integration. The finite product norm's unexpanded numerical formula introduces no unresolved effect on this statement.",
      "primary_evidence": "D018 uses IntegrableOn on both endpoint orientations; D083 subtracts the two restricted integrals. D050 defines subtraction componentwise, D054 gives the coordinate product topology, and D051–D053 supply compatible finite-dimensional normed structures. No norm-dependent bound occurs. The supplement identifies the integration measure explicitly."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C09 unclear",
      "resolution": "Constants and indexing pass. No hidden measure scaling remains. Spatial endpoint order, temporal orientation, unit coefficients, and all m vector components are preserved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target uses M(t)-M(s) and ∫ from s to t of flux(q(a,τ))-flux(q(b,τ)). D050 and D064 preserve subtraction order. The supplement's explicit Real.volume_Ioc fixes interval length as ENNReal.ofReal (b-a), and Fin m indexes the entire state vector."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exceptional and boundary cases pass under the recorded interpretation. Null exceptional times are ordinary Lebesgue-null and may depend on a,b. Reversed endpoints negate the corresponding identities consistently; coincident endpoints yield zero identities. Integrability excludes reliance on default values of nonintegrable integrals. Pointwise endpoint representatives remain subject to the rectangle condition.",
      "primary_evidence": "D083 explicitly implements orientation. D018 supplies integrability in either order. The target places ∀ a b outside the ae quantifier and uses the same Real.measureSpace.volume resolved by the supplement. Printed page 5 asserts continued integral conservation at discontinuities without defining representatives or traces."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "This implication is yes under the recorded user-adopted interpretation. The translation's μ is now identified with the intended real length measure. In the adopted conservation context A∧B∧C, its equivalence supplies D, exactly the interpreted mass-rate assertion. The equivalence alone does not assert conservation for arbitrary unrelated q and flux.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation reconstructs (A∧B∧C) ↔ (A∧B∧C∧D), agreeing with the target after unfolding D001. D is the correctly signed derivative of spatial mass for almost every time after fixing the interval. The source concerns conservation solutions, and the receipt supplies their rectangle interpretation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "This implication is yes under the recorded user-adopted interpretation. Its conservation context is A∧B∧C and its mass-rate assertion is D, giving the forward half of the translated equivalence. The reverse half merely projects A∧B∧C. No inference from an almost-everywhere derivative alone to rectangle balance is required.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 and the first three right-hand conjuncts coincide. For fixed a,b, the rectangle identity gives M(u)=M(c)+∫ from c to u of the endpoint flux difference. Temporal flux integrability makes this a locally absolutely continuous finite-dimensional mass function, whose derivative equals the flux difference almost everywhere. The supplement identifies the measure needed for this interpretation."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, applicability, and classification consistency",
      "resolution": "The conservation context is satisfiable in positive dimension and includes nonconstant, discontinuous solutions. The integrability conditions belong to the adopted interpretation and are not credited as stronger theorem content. The harmless m=0 extension does not remove positive-dimensional cases or justify a faithful-stronger classification. Both implication verdicts are yes, consistently yielding faithful-equivalent.",
      "primary_evidence": "Directly substituting m=1, q(x,t)=x-t and flux(v)=v into D001 gives both mass increment and integrated boundary flux equal to -(b-a)(t-s). A moving step q(x,t)=1 for x>t and 0 otherwise with identity flux also satisfies rectangle balance, with mass-rate exceptions at endpoint crossings. Conversely q(x,t)=t with zero flux violates the balance on nondegenerate rectangles. These checks use D001's supplied definition, not the target proof."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded user-adopted interpretation only, conservation solutionhood is D001's spatial integrability, temporal endpoint-flux integrability, and rectangle balance. The target's forward implication then supplies the actual derivative of spatial vector mass equal to first-endpoint flux minus second-endpoint flux for almost every time separately for each fixed interval. The supplement identifies its measure as ordinary real length measure. This recovers the selected equation's componentwise conservation meaning under that interpretation; it does not establish an everywhere-classical reading of the printed display."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded user-adopted interpretation only, the selected claim says that rectangle conservation with the explicit integrability conditions has the intervalwise almost-everywhere mass-rate property. Writing the rectangle conditions as R and the rate property as D, this is R → D. The exact Lean proposition unfolds to R ↔ (R ∧ D), equivalent to that conditional assertion. Its reverse half is projection, and its forward half imposes no extra state smoothness or common exceptional-time set. The zero-dimensional case is independently trivial. This implication is not asserted from the printed source without the recorded interpretation."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-equivalent",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The printed source alone leaves the temporal derivative sense, regularity class, endpoint representatives or traces, and explicit orientation conventions unspecified. This acceptance does not resolve those source-only ambiguities or attribute the adopted conventions to the book.",
    "The runtime provenance and hashes were inspected as supplied evidence; no source, rendering, dossier, binary, or compiled-module hashes were independently recomputed in this tool-free adjudication."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "resolved-measure-semantics",
      "evidence": "The native supplement explicitly connects the target's Real.measureSpace.volume to StieltjesFunction.id.measure and gives its interval-length normalization on borel Real.",
      "impact": "The D065 evidence gap and its dependent conclusion, operator, coefficient, exceptional-set, and implication uncertainties are resolved."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-qualified-acceptance",
      "evidence": "Printed pages 4–5 state the mass balance and its continued relevance at discontinuities without the analytic conventions explicitly supplied by the separate user receipt.",
      "impact": "Acceptance applies only to the selected equation under the recorded rectangle and intervalwise almost-everywhere interpretation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "logical-form-and-applicability",
      "evidence": "D001 expands to the first three right-hand conjuncts, so the target is R ↔ (R ∧ Rate). Positive-dimensional nonconstant and discontinuous examples satisfy R.",
      "impact": "The theorem establishes a nonvacuous mass-rate consequence of the adopted conservation property. It neither asserts conservation for arbitrary functions nor reconstructs rectangle conservation from an almost-everywhere derivative alone."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached source pages and inline declaration evidence resolves the disagreement without majority vote. The native supplement supplies the precise measure identity missing from the blind translation, including the exact selected instance and normalization. The remaining operators preserve spatial mass, temporal differentiation, vector components, endpoint signs, integrability, and interval-dependent exceptional times. Unfolding the local predicate confirms both implication directions under the recorded user-adopted interpretation, and positive-dimensional examples establish nonvacuity. Faithful-equivalent is therefore accepted within that interpretation, with the original printed-source ambiguity preserved."
}
